//   kKnee = j₀,₁/rMax ≈ 0.22–0.27 rad/cell. A HARD dot (_pdot, ~3×3) is nearly a delta, so its spectrum lives
//   ABOVE the knee in the dispersive band and isolated hard dots CANNOT form a coherent lock (speckle ~1.1 =
//   noise). A Gaussian with a finite waist sits BELOW the knee and locks coherently (speckle 0.78 ≈ letterA's
//   0.75). So point/pair/grid are kept for CONTRAST — they are supposed to decohere — while letterA/cross are
//   dense dot-chains whose density is the visible texture.
//   MEASURED, AND THE KNEE MOVES. kKnee = j0,1/rMax, and rMax is whatever the IFS cascade has produced so far:
//     ticks  40 -> r=[6,8,11,17]  kKnee 0.141      (what buildSlot samples — an EARLY, transient state)
//     ticks 200 -> r=[5,6,8,9]    kKnee 0.267      (settled — the top of mu1's own quoted 0.22-0.27)
//   So ahc and mu1 have essentially the SAME medium once the cascade settles; the difference is only where in
//   its life the ring is sampled. % of energy above the knee, at each:
//                 kKnee 0.141    kKnee 0.267
//     blob            0.3            0.2
//     packet          0.7            0.0
//     lightpts       83.2           19.3      <- coherent once settled, exactly as mu1 reports
//     letterA        82.7           71.7
//     grid           99.6           96.1
//   A FIRST VERSION OF THIS NOTE claimed "lightpts is not coherent here, that was mu1's ring" — wrong, and for
//   an instructive reason: I compared a settled mu1 number against an unsettled ahc one and read a difference
//   of MEDIUM where there was only a difference of AGE. packet is band-limited by construction, so it is the
//   one object that stays below the knee at either sampling (0.7% / 0.0%).
const OBJS = ["letterA", "cross", "ring", "blob", "depthscene", "lightpts", "packet", "beam", "point", "pair", "grid", "grating", "square", "disc", "triangle", "diamond", "void", "annulus", "wells", "junction", "cosine", "cube", "pyramid", "house", "torus"];   // void (2026-10-26): an EMPTY layer — a link layer of medium holds only the light that tunnels into it
//   SOLID SHAPES (2026-10-22, user: "for our medium it is better to work with solid objects"): □ square · ○ disc · △ triangle · ◇ diamond — the
//   depthscene's layers as objects of their own (one solid, uniform amplitude 0.9, radius 0.1·side ÷ v), centred in the region; compact and
//   low-|k| (the band the medium holds), sharp-edged (depth shows as blur). The pose turn is not applied to them (□ ○ ◇ are symmetric).
//   OBJECT PARAMETERS — every object carries ONE parameter of its own geometry in its NAME, "<obj>@<v>", so every path that carries the
//   replicated lensObj (the register, the dop, the slot's re-seed door, the moving-att regeneration, the renderer twin) carries it with no
//   new field; the bare name is the default and draws byte-identically to before. What v IS depends on the object — each its own scale:
//     packet   k0 as a fraction of the medium's knee (its carrier: the formant)                        0.2 … 2.5, default 0.7
//     grid     dots per side, period G/m on the torus (a 2D lattice: Bragg shells m·√(a²+b²) — a BELL)  2 … 16,   default 3
