             <div style="color:#79c0ff;margin-top:3px;" title="⚇ TWO PARTICLES IN ONE SLOT — ψ(x, y) on the G × G torus IS the exact wavefunction of two particles on a G-site ring (particle 1 = x, particle 2 = y; first quantization, exact — no approximation). The medium's own 2D step, read as two particles, carries a correlated hop (its diagonal stencil, the IFS rings' isotropy); ⚇sep DECLARES the separable kinetic (each particle hops by the medium's own 1D law). The contact interaction V(x − y) = U·e^{−(d/w)²} as a phase per sub-step (U > 0 attractive, < 0 repulsive — bound on top). Exchange symmetry across the diagonal: bosons / fermions / distinguishable. The image of the slot IS the pair correlation |ψ(x, y)|² (bosons bunch onto the diagonal, fermions vanish there). Entanglement = the Schmidt decomposition of ψ_xy, exact.">⚇ two particles · exact few-body</div>
